  <section>
    <h2>Formation</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Hierarchical Model</h3>
        <pre><code>Dark matter halos merge first
Gas falls into potential wells
Cooling and fragmentation
First stars form (Pop III)
Mergers drive evolution</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Mergers</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Merge Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Major merger: mass ratio < 1:3
Minor merger: mass ratio > 1:3
Dry merger: gas-poor, no star formation
Wet merger: gas-rich, starburst
Triggered star formation and AGN activity</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>AGN Feedback</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>AGN Types</h3>
        <pre><code>Quasar mode: luminous, accretion-powered
Radio mode: jet-powered, mechanical feedback
Quenching: AGN heats gas, prevents cooling
Self-regulation: AGN controls its own fuel</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Star Formation</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Kennicutt-Schmidt Law</h3>
        <pre><code>Σ_SFR ∝ Σ_gas^N
N ≈ 1.4 (power law index)
Σ_SFR: star formation rate surface density
Σ_gas: gas surface density</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Quenching</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Quenching Mechanisms</h3>
        <pre><code>Strangulation: gas supply cut off
Ram pressure stripping: galaxy moving through ICM
AGN feedback: heating from central black hole
Mergers: burst of star formation then quenching
Morphological quenching: bulge prevents instability</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

